This is my first post to RGRN.  I'm one of those eternal nethack dabblers,  
who's never persevered to ascension.

My question is: how does one maximize/optimize the desirable permanent  
intrinsics one could potentially acquire?  I suppose this depends on  
race/role and on the edibility of rings, etc, so what is the best  
character to start with, and should I scum until I get a particular ring,  
or anything?

What would this list of intrinsics look like, and what would be missing  
(or unavoidably based on luck, or tradeoffs with others)?  Fiddling a bit  
in wizmode, I currently have:

   You are fire resistant.
   You are cold resistant.
   You are sleep resistant.
   You are disintegration-resistant.
   You are shock resistant.
   You are poison resistant.
   You see invisible.
   You are telepathic.
   You have automatic searching.
   You have infravision.
   You can survive without air.
   You are fast.

What am I missing? (I can't have stealth or regeneration because those  
rings happen to be inedible, and I don't consider permanent invisibility  
"desirable".)

Of course, the followup question is: having gained as many desirable  
permanent properties as possible intrinsically, how do you fill the gaps  
with extrinsics, given that there will inevitably be tradeoffs (e.g. boots  
of speed vs jumping)?

Here, I am deprecating carrying extra inventory to swap extrinsics in and  
out; I'm just concerned with properties at a given moment of time (e.g.  
death or ascension).

